{"test":"text:nat_en.txt","n_prompt":113,"pp_s":4.628,"pp_ts":24.4173,"n_gen":128,"tg_ts":1.6086,"tg_total_ts":1.6064,"gen":"The wind came in the dark, and the sea was a black thing, a living thing, and the lighthouse was a small, bright eye in the middle of it. He had the radio on, but the only voice he heard was the wind. He wrote in the logbook: \"The sea is angry. The wind is angry. I am angry. I have not seen the sea like this in thirty-one winters.\"\nThe next morning, the sea was calm. The sun came out, and the gulls were back. The lighthouse keeper went down to the landing stage, and there, on the rocks, was a small"}
